(4720298, 680051, 41337, '<td valign="top">I like the simplicity of it. The silhouettes turn this from a specific family to a universal one. However, the main thing that holds this back for me is the lack of emotion. I don''t see enough happiness in this photo. That''s not easy to convey photographing silhouettes so there needs to be more emphasis paid on the composition to convey it. For example, if the child was being held up higher and a burst of light or sun rays was hitting the child it would begin to show emotion, that of pride and of happiness. Perhaps that''s a little over dramatic or would make it too staged look but I just use that example to illustrate a basic point. Good luck.</td>', 'I like the simplicity of it. The silhouettes turn this from a specific family to a universal one. However, the main thing that holds this back for me is the lack of emotion. I don''t see enough happiness in this photo. That''s not easy to convey photographing silhouettes so there needs to be more emphasis paid on the composition to convey it. For example, if the child was being held up higher and a burst of light or sun rays was hitting the child it would begin to show emotion, that of pride and of happiness. Perhaps that''s a little over dramatic or would make it too staged look but I just use that example to illustrate a basic point. Good luck.', '2008-05-23 17:29:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(4720323, 680112, 41337, '<td valign="top">I like how you cropped her head off. However in doing so the leading line leads you straight to her behind, which may not be a bad thing but it makes it more like a photo for a jeans ad. If that''s what you''re going for then this is perfect, I wouldn''t change a thing. If not then a landscape orientation would have been better, IMO. It would allow more of the road on the right to be shown and thus it would shift the leading line over to the right and that way it would guide the eye towards her destination rather than her behind, if that makes sense.</td>', 'I like how you cropped her head off. However in doing so the leading line leads you straight to her behind, which may not be a bad thing but it makes it more like a photo for a jeans ad. If that''s what you''re going for then this is perfect, I wouldn''t change a thing. If not then a landscape orientation would have been better, IMO. It would allow more of the road on the right to be shown and thus it would shift the leading line over to the right and that way it would guide the eye towards her destination rather than her behind, if that makes sense.', '2008-05-23 17:41:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(4720327, 679379, 41337, '<td valign="top">Nice action shot but you really needed to be on the other side to make this more effective (i.e. you would have captured their faces better).</td>', 'Nice action shot but you really needed to be on the other side to make this more effective (i.e. you would have captured their faces better).', '2008-05-23 17:42:08.000000', NULL, 1),
