(4729166, 680454, 93765, '<td valign="top">Obviously a polarizing picture...<br/> <br/>I am thrilled and grateful for the nines and tens, hadn''t expected those, but frankly a bit disappointed at the large number of ones and twos. Surely as a picture it wasn''t that bad...? So what, if you don''t know what you are looking at? In my book the important thing is: do I like what I see, never mind what it is or how it got there.<br/> <br/>Thank you all for taking the time to comment on it (particularly those going beyond an expression of mere puzzlement), I really appreciate it! The DNMC in a "use your fantasy" challenge I found somewhat uncalled for, though. That criterion should apply to viewers as well ;)<br/> <br/>(now how do I get this text up there in the "photographer''s comments" where it belongs...?)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-05-28 04:16:27.</i></td>', 'Obviously a polarizing picture... I am thrilled and grateful for the nines and tens, hadn''t expected those, but frankly a bit disappointed at the large number of ones and twos. Surely as a picture it wasn''t that bad...? So what, if you don''t know what you are looking at? In my book the important thing is: do I like what I see, never mind what it is or how it got there. Thank you all for taking the time to comment on it (particularly those going beyond an expression of mere puzzlement), I really appreciate it! The DNMC in a "use your fantasy" challenge I found somewhat uncalled for, though. That criterion should apply to viewers as well ;) (now how do I get this text up there in the "photographer''s comments" where it belongs...?)', '2008-05-28 05:01:36.000000', '2008-05-28 05:16:27.000000', 0),
