(4729224, 680454, 53572, '<td valign="top">tom, a great image.  you were one of my top scores - beautiful, creative and original.  you''ll find that dpc as a whole can be rather conservative in interpretation.  but, not all of us.  the <a href="//dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=624708" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">posthumous ribbons thread</a> goes a long way to redressing the egregiously misunderstood, and <a href="//dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=767571" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">team suck</a> is a great gathering place for the tangential.<br/> <br/>(ps, you''ll be in the posthumous ribbon thread in a bit, as you''re getting on of mine today (after the whole ironing, lunch making, getting them off to school thing)....  shhhhhh)<br/> <br/>o, yes, cick on the ''edit details of the image'' link in the...image details section.  then you can edit your comments.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-05-28 07:58:37.</i></td>', 'tom, a great image.  you were one of my top scores - beautiful, creative and original.  you''ll find that dpc as a whole can be rather conservative in interpretation.  but, not all of us.  the posthumous ribbons thread goes a long way to redressing the egregiously misunderstood, and team suck is a great gathering place for the tangential. (ps, you''ll be in the posthumous ribbon thread in a bit, as you''re getting on of mine today (after the whole ironing, lunch making, getting them off to school thing)....  shhhhhh) o, yes, cick on the ''edit details of the image'' link in the...image details section.  then you can edit your comments.', '2008-05-28 06:05:11.000000', '2008-05-28 08:58:37.000000', 0),
