(4729347, 678766, 77196, '<td valign="top">Glad to see you participating here. It tends to be a tough crowd, but that makes it all the better when you get good comments from people. <br/> <br/>I like what you "saw" - the shape and position of the orchid is nice. <br/> <br/>With non-DSLR cameras, you''ll want to avoid higher ISO settings - these add (typically) too much grain (noise) to the picture. I try to shoot everything for DPChallenge at ISO 64 - as low ISO as I can get. <br/> <br/>While people here tend to like out of focus foregrounds, your shot has too much out of focus foreground. They generally like the in-focus area to begin in the bottom 1/3 to mid-point in the picture, and then have the background out of focus as well. The non-DSLR cameras (at least my experience) have a tendency to focus on the background (wall in your case), and not on objects in the foreground. <br/> <br/>Again, glad to see you participating here, and looking forward to seeing more of your work.</td>', 'Glad to see you participating here. It tends to be a tough crowd, but that makes it all the better when you get good comments from people.  I like what you "saw" - the shape and position of the orchid is nice.  With non-DSLR cameras, you''ll want to avoid higher ISO settings - these add (typically) too much grain (noise) to the picture. I try to shoot everything for DPChallenge at ISO 64 - as low ISO as I can get.  While people here tend to like out of focus foregrounds, your shot has too much out of focus foreground. They generally like the in-focus area to begin in the bottom 1/3 to mid-point in the picture, and then have the background out of focus as well. The non-DSLR cameras (at least my experience) have a tendency to focus on the background (wall in your case), and not on objects in the foreground.  Again, glad to see you participating here, and looking forward to seeing more of your work.', '2008-05-28 08:39:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(4729348, 680499, 74979, '<td valign="top">for all your whining about this image, Enzo, you did really well!  and for what it''s worth,  this is perfect for the title and the challenge...very dramatic, with excellent POV<br/> <br/>Congrats on the ribbon!!</td>', 'for all your whining about this image, Enzo, you did really well!  and for what it''s worth,  this is perfect for the title and the challenge...very dramatic, with excellent POV Congrats on the ribbon!!', '2008-05-28 08:39:12.000000', NULL, 0),
